DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Back from the Dead Indoor Performance - All Saints Day
DESCRIPTION:The dead would like to have some words with you...the question of the night is: are you ready for your death? This is the indoor version of our Cemetery Walk.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/back-from-the-dead-indoor-performance-all-saints-day/22449/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventdayofthedead26287-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Day of the Dead
DESCRIPTION:Join The Radical for a celebration of Día de Muertos (Day of the Dead)\, a Mexican tradition that brings family\, friends\, and communities together to remember and honor loved ones who have passed\, while celebrating the joy of life and the memories that keep their spirits alive. We're bringing together craft cocktails\, delicious Mexican food from La Carreta Tortas y Tacos\, music\, and family-friendly activities for an afternoon and evening of food\, drink\, remembrance\, and community. What to expect: Craft cocktails from The Radical\, including special Día de Muertos-inspired offerings alongside our regular favorites. Authentic Mexican food from La Carreta\, serving up delicious food to enjoy throughout the celebration. Music and a festive atmosphere to bring people together throughout the day and evening. Family-friendly themed activities inspired by the colors\, creativity\, and traditions of Día de Muertos. A chance to gather and remember\, celebrating the people\, stories\, and connections that remain with us. Whether you're familiar with Día de Muertos traditions or discovering them for the first time\, we invite you to join us in celebrating the rich cultural heritage behind this occasion and the universal importance of remembering those who came before us. Bring your friends\, bring your family\, and come spend some time with your neighbors as we celebrate life\, memory\, and community in the heart of Brunswick.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/day-of-the-dead/26287/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfrederickcitymarket11348-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Frederick City Market
DESCRIPTION:The Frederick City Market is a local food and artisan market located in the historic district of Downtown Frederick\, Maryland. Join us on every Sunday from May through November. Parking is free on Sundays and there are usually plenty of spots on 7th Street and Market Street. You can park at Gravel and Grind (15 E 6th Street) and walk through the gap into the market lot.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/frederick-city-market/11348/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventgothicafternoontea3atheblackdoorteasociety26307-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Gothic Afternoon Tea: The Black Door Tea Society
DESCRIPTION:You are cordially invited to step beyond the Black Door… if you dare. Join us at The Banyan for an enchanting afternoon of gothic elegance\, delicate savories\, freshly served scones\, darkly decadent desserts\, and bottomless tea. Expect wickedly delicious bites\, hauntingly beautiful details\, and a few delightful surprises along the way. All ages welcome! Dress for the occasion\, if you dare. Gather your coven\, summon your favorite people\, and join us for an afternoon that’s equal parts elegant and eerie. Additional cocktails\, wine\, and menu items will be available for purchase. Reservations: 301-228-9181
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/gothic-afternoon-tea%3a-the-black-door-tea-society/26307/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventreleafagency26157-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Re-Leaf Agency
DESCRIPTION:A Multisensory Performance Prompting Reflection and Action Re-Leaf Agency invites you into an immersive environment of lush movement\, rich sounds\, provocative text\, and larger-than-life video projections of trees\, mushrooms\, ferns\, wildflowers\, and streams spanning multiple surfaces. The performers summon you into the woods\, amplifying all manner of small and precious flora and fauna\, to reveal a needed refuge. Re-Leaf Agency is a recruitment session disguised as a performance\, or maybe it’s a performance disguised as a recruitment session. Either way\, this is the last time in 2026 when you can join the Agency to become a keeper of the good. Three Re-Leaf Agents - two dancers and a recruitment officer - implore you to join them in navigating the turbulent times in which we find ourselves. Amidst the anxiety of an unraveling democracy and the impacts of a changing climate\, Re-Leaf Agency rekindles hope by taking the long view of the natural world. This multimedia piece is the culmination of several years documenting a sliver of earth on the edge of Maryland’s South Mountain\, during which time MAD Dance director Kit Clark experienced the solace of non-human time while walking and witnessing the land. Re-Leaf Agency shares that profound experience with others. Dancers Amanda Comi and Jeanna Riscigno join Clark in this one-of-a-kind performance.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/re-leaf-agency/26157/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsoundtosoul3arestorativeyogawithsoundbathandsoulcollagewithtaralemeriseandmelodyklemin26308-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Sound to Soul: Restorative Yoga with Sound Bath and SoulCollage with Tara Lemerise and Melody Klemin
DESCRIPTION:Rest. Receive. Create. Connect. In this unique workshop\, you will first tend to your nervous system and quiet your analytical brain with passive\, fully propped Restorative Yoga postures accompanied by a soothing sound bath. This sets the stage for you to tap into your inner knowing and creative capacity with SoulCollage\, a guided collaging activity where you will create your own oracle card and learn to give voice to the card for ongoing support along your path. This meaningful afternoon is the perfect blend of time for introspection and time to connect in community. You will leave you feeling rested\, resourced\, and inspired. All materials are provided. All artistic abilities welcome.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/sound-to-soul%3a-restorative-yoga-with-sound-bath-and-soulcollage-with-tara-lemerise-and-melody-klemin/26308/
END:VEVENT
