SUMMARY:Guided Exhibit Tours
DESCRIPTION:Experience the Museum of Frederick County History through a guided tour. Join the staff and volunteers who curated our 2026 exhibits as they explore our various galleries. Each tour is a unique experience based on the interests of the group and what special things staff wants to highlight that week. Descriptions of each week's tour can be found on the Heritage Frederick website\, which includes accessibility notes. Tours are included with admission!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/guided-exhibit-tours/25817/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjamiekayefirstfridays25206-20261106@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Jamie Kaye First Fridays
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Jamie Kaye’s First Fridays at Sandbox! Jamie is an incredibly talented local sensation who has played at venues all over Frederick and the surrounding area. She’ll be at Sandbox playing her high energy\, all star set including current and classic hits\, sprinkled in originals\, AND a little birdie told us she takes song requests. Jamie ALWAYS brings a fun time - you won’t want to miss it!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jamie-kaye-first-fridays/25206/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventrootstorest3aacuaromasleepsupportwithruxandrameinze26309-20261106@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Roots to Rest: AcuAroma Sleep Support with Ruxandra Meinze
DESCRIPTION:Step into a more intentional approach to rest with a 75-minute\, hands-on AcuAroma Therapy workshop that brings together the therapeutic traditions of essential oils and Traditional Chinese Medicine acupressure. Working with a carefully selected collection of high-quality organic essential oils\, you’ll be introduced to three specific oil and acupressure point pairings chosen to support relaxation and restorative sleep. Your facilitator will explore the therapeutic qualities of each oil\, the significance of the corresponding organ points\, and\, most importantly\, how these points relate to and work together as part of a larger practice. This is both a learning experience and a moment of self-pampering. You’ll have time to slow down\, work with the oils directly\, and learn a simple ritual you can return to whenever your body and mind need help transitioning into deeper rest. You’ll also leave with your own take-home collection of therapeutic oils\, along with a laminated reference card featuring images of the three acupressure points so you can confidently locate and practice them at home. The goal is not simply to experience the work in the room\, but to give you the knowledge\, tools\, and quality ingredients to make it part of your own evening ritual. No prior experience is needed. Come as you are\, and leave with a deeper understanding of how aromatic medicine and acupressure can be thoughtfully combined to support your wellbeing.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/roots-to-rest%3a-acuaroma-sleep-support-with-ruxandra-meinze/26309/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtheyaacshow24815-20261106@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:The YAAC Show
DESCRIPTION:The YAAC Show is every other Friday. A LIVE talk show produced by the creative team at the Y Arts Center. Join us for an evening of inspiration\, entertainment\, and community connection—powered by the YMCA’s Arts and Humanities initiatives. Every other Friday at 6:30pm. $10 at the door. Free for YMCA Members. Check IG @y_arts_center for interview and musical guest information.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-yaac-show/24815/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtolumide26100-20261106@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:TolumiDE
DESCRIPTION:TolumiDE delivers an intimate and uplifting live experience that blends soul\, Afropop\, Gospel\, and contemporary African rhythms. Born in Toronto\, shaped by Lagos\, and now based in the greater Washington\, D.C.–Maryland area\, she brings a rich multicultural energy to the stage through her signature sound\, weaving English and Yorùbá vocals with themes of joy\, faith\, love\, and cultural identity. TolumiDE’s performances are warm\, engaging\, and deeply connected\, moving effortlessly between reflective moments and joyful\, rhythmic grooves that invite audiences in. Drawing from her latest album\, Suya Soul \, and charting single “Throwback\,” she creates a space where tradition and modern sound meet\, encouraging audiences to feel\, move\, and connect. This is more than a concert—it’s a shared experience of rhythm\, storytelling\, and cultural celebration that resonates across generations. Learn more about TolumiDE on her official website. This show is part of New Spire Arts’ programming. New Spire Stages\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers an intimate venue for a memorable concert experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/tolumide/26100/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent2026exhibitsatmuseumoffrederickcountyhistory24908-20261107@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:2026 Exhibits at Museum of Frederick County History
DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
