DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Pour House Trivia at Sandbox Brewhouse
DESCRIPTION:Monday nights presented by Pour House Trivia are so ON! Every Monday\, 7-close. Bring a friend\, grab a beer\, and be prepared to test your knowledge with your host\, Ian\, from Pour House Trivia.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/pour-house-trivia-at-sandbox-brewhouse/23336/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcityoffrederickparks26rec3aseniorexercise24651-20261208@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261209
SUMMARY:City of Frederick Parks & Rec: Senior Exercise
DESCRIPTION:A full body class! Utilizing bands\, light weights and body weight exercises you will get a full body workout. Cardio and stretching are incorporated into this class to give you a well-rounded workout.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/city-of-frederick-parks-%26-rec%3a-senior-exercise/24651/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfirsttuesdaykaraoke26212-20261208@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261209
SUMMARY:First Tuesday Karaoke
DESCRIPTION:Your Tuesday night just got better… Join us every first Tuesday at 7PM for Sandbox Karaoke Night! Whether you're itching to sing your heart out to Whitney Houston or bring the energy with a crowd-pleasing Lady Gaga hit\, all voices and skill levels are welcome. The mic is open\, taps are flowing\, and vibes are right!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/first-tuesday-karaoke/26212/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfrederickcityparks26rec3asenioryoga24650-20261209@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261210
SUMMARY:Frederick City Parks & Rec: Senior Yoga
DESCRIPTION:A yoga class focused on stretching the body. Slow movements and long holds are emphasized in this class. Modifications are provided and welcome during your practice. All ages are welcome.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/frederick-city-parks-%26-rec%3a-senior-yoga/24650/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventgamenight24976-20261209@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261210
SUMMARY:Game Night
DESCRIPTION:Join us weekly and participate in a FREE poker tournament. Games start at 6:00pm and 8:00pm. Check out our large library of board games. Test your chess skill with a growing group of chess enthusiasts (all levels are welcome). Happy Hour Specials: $3 Beef Tacos\, $3 canned beer\, & $5 Margarita's
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/game-night/24976/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent2026exhibitsatmuseumoffrederickcountyhistory24908-20261210@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
SUMMARY:2026 Exhibits at Museum of Frederick County History
DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventboardgamenight23706-20261210@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261101T164417Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
SUMMARY:Board Game Night
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Sandbox for Board Game Night! Every Thursday evening at 6PM. Learn a new game from local board game enthusiast Michael Southers and stay to play! The games are provided\, and Michael’s easy going style makes games approachable to new players for the evening. First come\, first served. Alternatively\, feel free to come out with friends to play your own game to be around others with a shared interest.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/board-game-night/23706/
END:VEVENT
